# CCO Performance Architecture

## Client data layer

- Use `window.ArcanaCcoData` / `CcoRequestCache` — **not** TanStack Query or React Query.
- Stale times live in `app/cco-cache-policy.js` (`STATIC`, `WORKLIST`, `PATIENT_LIST`, `JOURNAL`, `CALENDAR`, `ANALYTICS`).
- Instrument fetch via `app/cco-fetch-instrumentation.js`; verify with `window.__getFetchStats()` alongside `window.__getRenderStats()`.

## Consolidated endpoints (prefer over N+1)

- Customers view: `GET /api/v1/cco/staff/customers-shell`
- Calendar: `GET /api/v1/cco-bookings/calendar-bundle?fromDate&toDate`
- Analytics: `GET /api/v1/cco/staff/dashboard-snapshot` (fallback to individual monitor routes)
- Patient detail (no journal): `GET /api/v1/cco-patient-master/patient/summary`
- Journal lazy: `GET /api/v1/cco-journal/entries?patientId&limit&offset`

## Server cache (Redis + memory)

- Use `src/infra/ccoReadCache.js` for short-TTL read caches.
- **Never** cache full journal content cross-user in Redis.
- Journal remains lazy-loaded, private per session; `JOURNAL` policy uses `staleTime: 0`.

## Lists

- Patient list virtual scroll: `app/cco-patient-list-virtual.js` (threshold 80 rows).
- Mail queue virtual scroll: existing `lit-switchover.js` pattern (>150).

## Before claiming perf regressions

1. Run `npm run verify:cco-performance-baseline-prod` (or local equivalent).
2. Check DevTools: `__getFetchStats()` dedupe/cache hits.
3. Rebuild bundle after app.js / manifest changes: `npm run build:bundle`.

## QA checklist

- [ ] Hard reload `/admin#cco` — mail list clickable <200ms
- [ ] Customers shell: one `customers-shell` request on first visit (not separate stats+patients+templates)
- [ ] Patient detail opens without journal payload until Journal tab
- [ ] Calendar month: one `calendar-bundle` per range (not separate slots+cases+signals)
- [ ] `node scripts/rebuild-cco-indexes.js` after bulk patient/booking imports
